{#
	ACF layout: stack_list — Figma `content` (2098:238) on `about`, first drawn
	as `stack-list` (15:74).

	A `section-header` and a wrapping row of tool names. The chips are text, not
	links — nothing here filters anything — and they are not the `tag-chip`
	component: the frame fills them with `surface/raised` and sets them in
	Mono/Label.

	`role="list"` because the stylesheet removes the markers, and Safari drops
	list semantics from a list with no visible markers.

	The row starts on the start edge on its own: flex packs to `flex-start`,
	which is the right under dir="rtl". Each tool is its own item, so a Latin
	name never reorders the Hebrew around it.
#}

{% if section.items|length %}
	<section class="stack-list">
		<div class="container stack-list__inner">

			{% include 'partials/ui/section-header.twig' with {
				eyebrow: section.eyebrow,
				heading: section.heading,
				intro: section.intro
			} only %}

			<ul class="stack-list__items" role="list">
				{% for item in section.items %}
					{% if item.label %}
						<li class="stack-list__item">{{ item.label }}</li>
					{% endif %}
				{% endfor %}
			</ul>

		</div>
	</section>
{% endif %}
